   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.4. Increased capacity of Member States to provide adequate labour protection to workers in diverse forms of work arrangements, including on digital labour platforms, and in informal employment</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">- On 22 December 2022, the Law no 353/2022 was adopted. It amends several normative acts including the Law on the national social insurance system (Law 489/1999). [See in particular the results reported under 8.1 which includes the development by the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection of a voucher system to facilitate the formalization of daily labourers in agriculture]

- On 8 December 2022, Law 355/2022 which allows labour inspectors to conduct unannounced visits to tackle undeclared work was passed. Since then the State Labour Inspectorate (SLI) has improved its capability to exercise its new powers by enhancing its skills and upgrading its case management system and risk assessment tools. - On 4 November 2022, the ILO participated as primary technical source at the conference &quot;Moldova turns white: Solutions to encourage the transition to legal work&quot; organized by the MLSP.
- Between April and May, 2023 the ILO provided technical support for the implementation of a communication campaign to boost the image of the MLSP, promote a new institutional image of the State Labour Inspectorate and a new employer branding to attract young talent for the newly reformed labour inspectorate.  As result, 400 applications were collected and 16 new labour inspectors were hired, including 7 female inspectors.
- On 17 January 2022, the ILO organized a virtual tripartite workshop to validate the main findings and recommendations of the functional analysis of the organizational structures and operational procedures of the Labour Inspectorate done by the ILO in 2021. In March 29-31, 2022 the ILO organized a virtual training course for 80 labour inspectors to increase their knowledge and skills to tackle undeclared work.</narrative>
   </description>
