  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.4. Increased capacity of Member States to provide adequate labour protection to workers in diverse forms of work arrangements, including on digital labour platforms, and in informal employment</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">A comprehensive legal analysis of Moldovan legislation dealing with nonstandard forms of work (NSFW), including temporary work, part-time and on-call work and multiparty employment, was undertaken, and the results were published in November 2023.   The analysis covered the three issues cited above from the legal point of view and provided key statistics on them. 
Some of the key highlights in relation to non-standard forms of work, was to extend the personal scope of protection of the Labour Code; extend the NSFW regulated in the Labour Code by including the temporary agency institution; consider the regulation of digital platform work; clarify the definition of undeclared work, work with no employment contract, disguised self-employed, disguised fixed-term of part-time employment. The results were validated by the government in a tripartite workshop held in September 2023 in Chisinau and key recommendations were included in the National Program to tackle undeclared work. The ILO supported the production of the legal analysis and provided technical guidance throughout its production phases. The ILO also participated in the validation workshop in September 2023.</narrative>
   </description>
